Subject: [PATCH 035/154] refactor: rename the nineteen portable .mm files to
 .cc
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

None of these contains a single line of Objective-C - no #import, no @
directive, no NS type. They were portable C++ wearing the wrong extension,
which is what kept the atrium sources inside the is_mac block.

Ten could have moved before H2; the other nine were waiting on the controller
header, which an earlier change cleaned. The list was re-derived from the tree rather
than taken from the task note, and it came back the same nineteen.

Both BUILD.gn source lists move in this commit. 28 comment references to the
old .mm paths are rewritten too, including each file's own first line - a
comment naming a file that does not exist is a small lie that survives a long
time.

chrome and unit_tests build with zero errors and zero warnings.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
